# System specification file
#
# Simulation of a CARBON DIOXIDE molecule in CARBON TETRACHLORIDE 
# with Kihara potential (the third parameters shoul be turned to zero
# if in the beginning the bad configuration is given)
#
# Input units in Stisu are amu, angstrom and 0.1ps 
# so the energy dimension parameters must be in kJ/mole
# and the length dimension parameters must be in angstrom
#
# Input string should be less 128 symbols
# 
CarbonDioxide 1
#
# The Chedin's potential with 28 parameters is used here for CO2
# (see Chedin A. and Teffo J.-L. J.Mol.Spectrosc. 107(1984)333)
#
POT chedin2 
1 2 3  8.49441 4.01316 14.7322
POT chedin34
1 2 3  -0.169658 -0.349882 -0.915698 -0.00309579 0.00762742 -0.0349418 0.00988316 -0.0332545 -0.0148403 
POT chedin5
1 2 3  0.000567461 0.000109297 0.00727883 -0.00135831 -0.00149995 0.00120956
POT chedin6
1 2 3  2.53031e-5 -1.00491e-3 -1.23064e-3 -1.06667e-4 -5.10572e-4 -1.67567e-3 8.90746e-5 -1.3157e-4 -1.08281e-5 -1.38092e-4
END_POT
# Atom C must be first
1	0	0	0	12	0	C 
2	0	0.15	1.3	16	0	O
2	0	0	-1.10
Tetrachloride 216
3	0	0	0	153.84	0	CCl4
end
#
# Kihara potential with 3 parameters is used 
# for C-CCl4, O-CCl4 and CCl4-CCl4 interactions.
# Parameters: 4 epsilon (kJ/mole), sigma (Angstroem) and a (Angstroem)
#
Kihara
1 3	 6.75	4.35	1.10 
2 3	 7.81	4.15	1.05 
3 3	18.3	5.30	1.80 # parameters are in respect with TD data
end
